---
import MediaFrame from "./ProductMediaFrame.astro";
import MerchandisingSystemGraphic from "./MerchandisingSystemGraphic.astro";
import businessSummary from "../assets/merchandising/graphics/merch-business-summary.png";
import editingWriteback from "../assets/merchandising/graphics/merch-editing-writeback.png";
import yearOverYear from "../assets/merchandising/graphics/merch-year-over-year.png";
---

<div class="merch-deep-content">
  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>06.1</span><div><p>Origin and business context</p><h3>The business already had a detailed plan. It did not have a shared way to understand it.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="two-column-copy">
      <div><h4>Information was concentrated in the sheet</h4><p>The planning spreadsheet combined promotions, product launches, email, SMS, homepage content, paid media, and historical planning. Teams familiar with its structure could work directly from it; other teams often needed help interpreting the same information.</p></div>
      <div><h4>The opportunity was easier access</h4><p>I saw an opportunity to make the plan easier to understand and use without disrupting the merchandising workflows already built around the spreadsheet. I created the application over a few weeks in June 2026 and continued testing and improving it after launch.</p></div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>06.2</span><div><p>Source-of-truth decision</p><h3>Preserve the working data system. Change the experience around it.</h3></div></header>
    <p class="chapter-intro">Some upstream information already populated the Google Sheet. Replacing it would have duplicated a working source, introduced synchronization risk, and created another system to maintain.</p>
    <MerchandisingSystemGraphic />
    <div class="decision-note"><strong>Keep the system of record. Redesign how people experience it.</strong><p>The application reads from the existing sheet. Controlled editing writes approved changes back to that same source.</p></div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>06.3</span><div><p>Information architecture and brand views</p><h3>The interface reorganizes planning data around the questions people are trying to answer.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="two-column-copy">
      <div><h4>Time and activity</h4><p>A visual timeline brings promotions into a scannable sequence. A dedicated product-launch lane and email schedule separate important activity that was difficult to follow inside the source sheet.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Context and retrieval</h4><p>Brand-specific views, content details, a business summary, search, and year-over-year comparisons help teams narrow the plan to the information relevant to their work.</p></div>
    </div>
    <MediaFrame label="Today at a Glance business summary">
      <img src={businessSummary.src} width={businessSummary.width} height={businessSummary.height} alt="Marketing Planner business summary showing current, recently ended, and upcoming activity." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </MediaFrame>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>06.4</span><div><p>Permissions and editing workflow</p><h3>Self-service visibility does not require uncontrolled changes.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="two-column-copy">
      <div><h4>Easy to view, controlled editing</h4><p>More people can view the planning information, while editing stays controlled. Permissions and the editing workflow determine how changes move back to the existing spreadsheet.</p></div>
      <div><h4>One maintained record</h4><p>Write-back keeps updates connected to the same source already used by merchandising and upstream processes. The application improves access without creating a parallel planning database.</p></div>
    </div>
    <MediaFrame label="Controlled editing and spreadsheet write-back">
      <img src={editingWriteback.src} width={editingWriteback.width} height={editingWriteback.height} alt="Controlled editing form that appends a new planning row to the existing Google Sheet." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </MediaFrame>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>06.5</span><div><p>Daily review and historical planning</p><h3>The plan connects to the creative work that actually went live.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="two-column-copy">
      <div><h4>Daily use</h4><p>Merchandising uses the application daily. Other teams can review promotions, launches, email activity, and brand information without first asking the teams closest to the sheet.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Historical screenshot record</h4><p>A daily homepage screenshot history connects the calendar plan to the live creative. That record gives future planning a visual reference for what ran previously, not just what was scheduled.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="history-flow" role="img" aria-label="Calendar plan connects to the actual live homepage creative and then informs future year-over-year planning."><div><span>01</span><strong>Calendar plan</strong></div><i>→</i><div><span>02</span><strong>Actual live creative</strong></div><i>→</i><div><span>03</span><strong>Future planning</strong></div></div>
    <div class="automation-context">
      <div><p>Related automation</p><h4>GitHub automations maintain the screenshot archive.</h4></div>
      <p>The automated screenshot grabber did not have the required Vercel bypass permissions for direct access. The related workflow captures screenshots through GitHub automations, with the resulting archive hosted through a company Gmail account.</p>
    </div>
    <MediaFrame label="Year-over-year planning comparison">
      <img src={yearOverYear.src} width={yearOverYear.width} height={yearOverYear.height} alt="Marketing Planner comparing the current planning week with the corresponding week from the previous year." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </MediaFrame>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>06.6</span><div><p>Leadership use and daily impact</p><h3>The team continues to use the tool to present merchandising plans to the VP of Marketing.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="impact-strip">
      <div><strong>Daily</strong><span>merchandising use</span></div>
      <div><strong>More teams</strong><span>can find planning information on their own</span></div>
      <div><strong>Ongoing</strong><span>presentation use with the VP of Marketing</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="estimate"><strong>Approximately 10–20 minutes of back-and-forth may be removed from common information requests.</strong> This is an estimate, not a measured time study.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>06.7</span><div><p>Future analytics and performance</p><h3>The next question moves from visibility toward learning.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="future-comparison">
      <div><span>Current</span><strong>What are we doing?</strong><p>Make the active plan visible, searchable, and easier to understand.</p></div>
      <div><span>Future plan</span><strong>What did we do last year, and how did it perform?</strong><p>Add performance information to the year-over-year view. This remains future work.</p></div>
    </div>
  </article>
</div>

<style>
  .merch-deep-content { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .deep-chapter > header p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .deep-chapter > header h3 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step-2); }
  .two-column-copy { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-7); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .two-column-copy h4 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .two-column-copy p, .chapter-intro { color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .chapter-intro { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .decision-note { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(13rem, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 0.6fr); gap: var(--space-5); margin-top: var(--space-5); padding: var(--space-5); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-canvas); }
  .decision-note p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .deep-chapter :global(.media-frame) { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .history-flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-3); align-items: center; margin-block: var(--space-6); padding: var(--space-5); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .history-flow div { display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .history-flow span { color: var(--color-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; }
  .history-flow i { color: var(--color-accent); font-style: normal; }
  .automation-context { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(13rem, 0.38fr) minmax(0, 0.62fr); gap: var(--space-6); padding: var(--space-5); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-canvas); }
  .automation-context p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .automation-context div p { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .automation-context h4 { margin: 0; }
  .impact-strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .impact-strip div { display: flex; min-height: 9rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .impact-strip div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .impact-strip strong { margin-top: auto; color: var(--color-accent); font-size: var(--step-2); }
  .impact-strip span { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .estimate { margin: 0; padding: var(--space-5); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 5%, transparent); color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .estimate strong { color: var(--color-text); }
  .future-comparison { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .future-comparison > div { padding: var(--space-6); }
  .future-comparison > div + div { border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 5%, transparent); }
  .future-comparison span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .future-comparison strong { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-4); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .future-comparison p { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .two-column-copy, .decision-note, .automation-context, .future-comparison { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .future-comparison > div + div { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-left: 0; }
    .impact-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .impact-strip div { min-height: 7rem; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .impact-strip div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .history-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .history-flow i { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  }
</style>
